			remediationAction: `${seconds < MAX_GHIDRA_DECOMPILE_TIMEOUT_SECONDS ? `Set REA_GHIDRA_DECOMPILE_TIMEOUT_SECONDS above ${String(seconds)} seconds (maximum ${String(MAX_GHIDRA_DECOMPILE_TIMEOUT_SECONDS)}), or unset it to leave decompilation unbounded,` : `REA_GHIDRA_DECOMPILE_TIMEOUT_SECONDS is already at its maximum of ${String(seconds)} seconds; unset it to leave decompilation unbounded`} in the environment of a new REA invocation, then rerun the command. That invocation starts a new Ghidra session and ${ghidraSessionRestart(existingProject)}. Use \`rea function\` for this procedure's listing facts without pseudocode.`,
			continuingRemediationAction: "Use analyze_function (CLI: `rea function`) for listing facts. Call update_analysis_settings with setting ghidra.decompile_timeout_seconds and action set to raise the per-function deadline for the next operation on this Program. For CLI or future REA processes, set REA_GHIDRA_DECOMPILE_TIMEOUT_SECONDS. Set the MCP tool-call deadline to cover startup and the full call; earlier cancellation closes the session. `rea setup` estimates deadlines for new Codex/Kimi registrations and preserves existing positive values; edit existing deadlines yourself."
